  "intro": "Charlotte is a big airline hub in a part of the country this site otherwise skips entirely. The airport is a major connecting hub with constant traffic, the Piedmont rolls gently enough that VHF carries well in every direction, and the Catawba chain of lakes puts recreational marine traffic close to the city. Inland from here the Blue Ridge escarpment rises within two hours, and the repeaters on it are audible from the city on a good day.",
